/-!
# Sylow alternatives and the small-center reduction in §16.5

The exact targets retain the canonical H/K projections, actual relative
Sylow subgroups, relative normality and normalizing conjugators.
The completed center reduction uses a disjoint conjugate to force |Z_C| = 2
and then applies 16.5.2(1) to obtain a conjugator normalizing the full T.

Construction of the two Sylow alternatives and completion of the derived-center
contradiction remain obligations. No source-numbered theorem is asserted from
an output record or from the definitions of these targets.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004, Lemmas
16.5.2(2) and 16.5.7, printed pp.1195 and 1197–1198.
-/
